Note: grades with a table of lists and a function of your own.

to find the letter for a score
  if the score is at least 90, give back "A".
  if the score is at least 80, give back "B".
  if the score is at least 70, give back "C".
  give back "F".
that's all.

the scores of "Ana" are 95, 88 and 92.
the scores of "Bob" are 72, 65 and 80.
the scores of "Dana" are 85, 91 and 78.

for every student in the scores
  set average to (the average of the scores of student) rounded.
  say student and then ":" and then average and then "points, grade" and then the letter for average.
that's all.

set everyone to an empty list.
for every student in the scores
  for every score in the scores of student, add score to everyone.
that's all.
sort everyone.
say "All scores from low to high:" and then everyone joined with ", ".
say "Best score:" and then the largest of everyone.
